facts:
Each new InType must be added in four places:
- main.c event_name, whose table has a static assert on its size (src/main.c:80-87);
- power_asleep_drops, which drops TOUCH_* and PINCH_BEGIN/MOVE while asleep but lets PINCH_END through (src/power.c:80-94);
- the BOOK_RUNNING guard (src/app.c:462);
- note_input (src/app.c:464).

constraints:
Existing behavior to keep:
- the pinch dead zone (k_pinch_gate.qs);
- the 400 ms late-second-finger palm rule for zoom;
- tap = lift within 30 px slop;
- link hold 600 ms;
- the pinch_zoom toggle disabling zoom only, while two-finger gestures still work;
- pinch ignored inside the Pages view;
- tap outside a sheet dismisses it and swallows the gesture.

Reserved, not assignable in record mode:
- one-finger tap and one-finger hold (UI, links, the hotbar's tap and long press);
- two-finger spread or squeeze while pinch zoom is on;
- two-finger sideways drag where the view can pan (always in landscape at default zoom, and whenever zoomed).

opportunities:
Two-finger classification at the existing dead-zone commit. Let spread_px = |d - d0| and trans = |mid - mid0|.
- spread_px >= ~0.6*trans: ZOOM (today's pinch, if enabled).
- Otherwise TRANSLATE:
  - PAN, with the zoom held at its commit value so drags stop wobbling the zoom, if the editor's view context says it can pan along the dominant axis in that direction;
  - EDGE SWIPE if the midpoint started within ~15 mm of an edge and moves inward;
  - otherwise SWIPE.
- A swipe fires at the first lift if:
  - travel is at least ~20 mm (about 236 px);
  - the angle is within about 30 degrees of an axis;
  - both fingers moved the same way (cosine at least 0.8) by similar amounts (ratio 0.5 to 2);
  - it took no more than ~1 s.
- The editor pushes its context (can pan +x, -x, +y, -y; pinch_zoom; gestures on; record mode) whenever view_clamp changes ox, oy or zoom.
- Result for the owner's defaults: upright and fitted, a two-finger drag down anywhere opens Pages. In landscape or zoomed it pans, unless it starts in the top band or the view is already at its top limit. Bottom-edge-up opens the hotbar everywhere.

A fixed gesture list keeps the record mode reliable: fingers {1, 2, 3} x {tap, double tap, hold, swipe up/down/left/right, edge swipe from top/bottom/left/right}, minus the reserved items. Timing:
- landing window of 150 ms for 2 fingers and 250 ms for 3 (the logs put 79% of cancelled two-finger landings within 150 ms; measure deliberate 3-finger landings);
- an N-finger tap lasts 300 ms or less, every finger travels 5 mm or less, and the lifts fall within 150 ms of each other;
- hold 600 ms with 3 mm or less of movement (LINK_HOLD_MS and ROW_HOLD_MS);
- double tap gap 350 ms, as the owner's pen ruling. Only an action that has a double bound waits, and a gesture whose count is bound alone fires at once, as in the pen plan.
- Fire on lift by default. The cost is about 13-30 ms, and it lets a reversed drag cancel. Holds and pending doubles resolve in editor_tick only when the last batch drained the input (the pen plan's App.input_drained), so a lift still queued is never misread as a hold.

False-positive guards for a hand resting while writing (hand repositioning more than 1 s after the pen left), checked on every frame:
- contacts ever flagged MT_TOOL_PALM;
- large TOUCH_MAJOR;
- unequal contact sizes;
- non-parallel motion;
- travel under ~20 mm, or a slow settle;
- contacts below and to the writing-hand side of the last pen point.
If any guard trips, the multi-contact session becomes suppressed, as today.

Headless runner commands that feed contacts, at 13 ms per frame, through touchgest.c:
- 'finger ID down|move|up X Y [TOOL] [MAJOR]', one frame per line or grouped;
- 'swipe N X Y DX DY STEPS [SEP] [LANDGAP]';
- 'tapn N X Y [SEP] [MS]';
- the existing 'pen hover' and 'pen leave' drive the pen context.
Probes: touch.gesture (the last key), touch.reject (the last reason), touch.contacts, editor.hotbar. Keep 'pinch' and 'tap' working unchanged at first, so existing scenarios stay green.

Simulator window:
- Shift plus right-drag = two fingers 25 mm apart moving together;
- Alt plus right-drag = three fingers;
- Ctrl plus right-click = a two-finger tap;
- the mouse wheel stays the pinch.
- Optionally map SDL3 SDL_EVENT_FINGER_* from a Mac trackpad onto the panel. This needs checking on macOS: whether SDL3 delivers trackpad touches, and with what coordinates.

risks:
Record-mode pitfalls:
- recording with looser thresholds than runtime records gestures that later fail;
- free-form templates (shape matching) are unreliable with 75 Hz centroids and palms;
- a silent refusal while the pen hovers looks like a hang. Today every touch on every screen is refused while the pen is near, Settings included.

specs.angle:
CALM AND DISCOVERABLE. A first-time owner should understand everything without a manual, on e-ink. Seven rules carry the design:

1. THE PAGE IS HOME. Every link task happens over the page that stays in view: making, following, renaming, retargeting, deleting, browsing and searching. Only the Pages view and the new Index map are full screen, and the user opens both on purpose.
2. EVERY GESTURE HAS A VISIBLE, LABELLED TWIN:
   - two fingers down = the panel's page chip (exists);
   - two fingers up = a new Links button on the panel;
   - two fingers left/right = the panel's arrows;
   - the eye, Go to, New link and Index map are labelled buttons in the Links bar;
   - Smart shapes = a panel button plus a labelled toggle in the tool picker.
3. ONE MEANING PER INPUT. The pen draws (and presses UI, as today). One finger taps or holds: links and UI. Two fingers navigate, or zoom and pan. Nothing new happens under a resting pen or palm, and gestures fire only on lift.
4. PREVIEW BEFORE COMMIT:
   - a shape snap is a preview until the pen lifts, and moving on cancels it;
   - a new link's area shows dotted before it is saved;
   - a jump from the Links bar is a peek, with Back and Stay always on screen.
5. MODES ARE VISIBLE AND SHOW THEIR WAY OUT. Link mode keeps a top banner with Cancel. A peek has a header with Back. Recording a gesture has a card with Cancel and a reason for every try it refuses.
6. UNDO COVERS IT. Making, deleting, retargeting a link and every snapped shape are each one Undo step, in line with the owner's one-gesture-one-moment rule.
7. TEACH ONCE, GENTLY. Six one-time tips are toasts that never block, plus the hint line in the Links bar header. Defaults that could surprise stay unbound: no two-finger-tap undo, no one-finger swipes.

The price of calm: a 12th and 13th panel button, labelled icons in the bar, and an edge rule for navigation swipes on views that can scroll.

